signin.vue:

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
useSeoMeta({ title: 'Sign in — Payvand' })

const route = useRoute()
const router = useRouter()
const { signin, ensureSession } = useAuth()

const email = ref('')
const password = ref('')
const failure = ref('')
const busy = ref(false)

const nextPath = computed(() => safeNextPath(route.query.next))

async function submit() {
  failure.value = ''
  if (!email.value.trim()) { failure.value = 'Enter your email address.'; return }
  if (!password.value) { failure.value = 'Enter your password.'; return }

  busy.value = true
  try {
    await signin(email.value, password.value)
    await router.replace(nextPath.value)
  } catch (error) {
    failure.value = errorMessage(error, 'Could not sign in.')
  } finally {
    busy.value = false }
}
</script>
```

Need an `errorMessage` helper. Let me look at how other pages do it: `error instanceof Error ? error.message : '...'`. For $fetch errors, `error.message` includes stuff like "FetchError: [POST] ..." — ugly. $fetch errors have `data` with the server's error body. ApiError serializes how? Let me check payments.rs ApiError — it likely derives thiserror with thiserror::Error and a IntoResponse that returns JSON {error: "..."}. Let me check payments.rs to get the shape of error responses so I can extract `error.data.error`.

