## Accounts

Email + password with your own database, and `users.wallet` left nullable as the slot for Solana sign-in later — exactly the split you picked.

**API** ([server/src/auth.rs](server/src/auth.rs), [server/src/db.rs](server/src/db.rs))

| Route | Behaviour |
|---|---|
| `POST /api/auth/signup` | normalizes/validates email, Argon2id hash, rejects duplicates |
| `POST /api/auth/signin` | one generic message for both "no such user" and "wrong password" |
| `POST /api/auth/signout` | revokes the bearer session |
| `GET /api/auth/me` | the signed-in account |

Sessions are 32 random bytes held 30 days. Only the SHA-256 digest is stored, so a leaked database dump can't be replayed as a live session. With no `DATABASE_URL` set it uses embedded SQLite at `data/payvand.db` and migrates on startup; point it at a Turso-compatible libSQL server in production and it works unchanged inside a serverless isolate.

